{"text":"**The rule that came out of it, which is now enforced:** an alternative may\ndiffer ONLY in the predicate. Both endpoints must name the same entity. Surface\nvariation is normalisation's job; predicate variation is expected and fine,\n`works_for` vs `member_of`, `born_in` vs `grew_up_in`. Renaming an endpoint is a\ndifferent node and a different claim.","range":{"byteOffset":{"start":7731,"end":8081},"start":{"line":171,"column":0},"end":{"line":175,"column":37}},"file":"/tmp/aimee-s1-b06-production-5ox9qqoh/work/bench/tier-a/MEASUREMENT_LOG.md","lines":"**The rule that came out of it, which is now enforced:** an alternative may\ndiffer ONLY in the predicate. Both endpoints must name the same entity. Surface\nvariation is normalisation's job; predicate variation is expected and fine,\n`works_for` vs `member_of`, `born_in` vs `grew_up_in`. Renaming an endpoint is a\ndifferent node and a different claim.","charCount":{"leading":0,"trailing":0},"language":"Markdown"}
{"text":"`MF_CONF_FLOOR` (0.6) discards any fact below the threshold. Scoring with it\napplied conflates two different things, whether a model can extract the fact,\nand whether it emits a usable confidence, and the conflation falls almost\nentirely on small models:","range":{"byteOffset":{"start":10483,"end":10737},"start":{"line":224,"column":0},"end":{"line":227,"column":25}},"file":"/tmp/aimee-s1-b06-production-5ox9qqoh/work/bench/tier-a/MEASUREMENT_LOG.md","lines":"`MF_CONF_FLOOR` (0.6) discards any fact below the threshold. Scoring with it\napplied conflates two different things, whether a model can extract the fact,\nand whether it emits a usable confidence, and the conflation falls almost\nentirely on small models:","charCount":{"leading":0,"trailing":0},"language":"Markdown"}
{"text":"**Gold triples no model produces.** If 23 models all miss the same labelled fact,\nthe label is the likelier error. Exactly one triple qualified:\n`am05 ingrid|has_role|manager` from \"My manager's manager is Ingrid.\" The models\nproduced ten different readings, none more than twice, none matching the label.\nIngrid is not \"a manager\" in the has_role sense, she is two levels up a reporting\nchain whose intermediate entity is unresolved, and the ontology has no reporting\nrelation. Now empty, alongside the other ambiguous items.","range":{"byteOffset":{"start":12230,"end":12756},"start":{"line":262,"column":0},"end":{"line":268,"column":57}},"file":"/tmp/aimee-s1-b06-production-5ox9qqoh/work/bench/tier-a/MEASUREMENT_LOG.md","lines":"**Gold triples no model produces.** If 23 models all miss the same labelled fact,\nthe label is the likelier error. Exactly one triple qualified:\n`am05 ingrid|has_role|manager` from \"My manager's manager is Ingrid.\" The models\nproduced ten different readings, none more than twice, none matching the label.\nIngrid is not \"a manager\" in the has_role sense, she is two levels up a reporting\nchain whose intermediate entity is unresolved, and the ontology has no reporting\nrelation. Now empty, alongside the other ambiguous items.","charCount":{"leading":0,"trailing":0},"language":"Markdown"}
{"text":"**Categories with no gold triples report null, not 0.** transient, and most of\nambiguous and negation, have no gold triples, so P/R/F1 are undefined there.\nReporting 0.0 inverted the meaning, fp=0 on a factless note is perfect\nrestraint, and a chart would have shown it as the worst category. Read\n`abstention_rate_on_schema` for those instead.","range":{"byteOffset":{"start":17344,"end":17688},"start":{"line":358,"column":0},"end":{"line":362,"column":46}},"file":"/tmp/aimee-s1-b06-production-5ox9qqoh/work/bench/tier-a/MEASUREMENT_LOG.md","lines":"**Categories with no gold triples report null, not 0.** transient, and most of\nambiguous and negation, have no gold triples, so P/R/F1 are undefined there.\nReporting 0.0 inverted the meaning, fp=0 on a factless note is perfect\nrestraint, and a chart would have shown it as the worst category. Read\n`abstention_rate_on_schema` for those instead.","charCount":{"leading":0,"trailing":0},"language":"Markdown"}
{"text":"`sweep_b.sh gpu` and `sweep.sh`'s llamacpp arm write to a directory named `gpu`\nand pass no `-ngl`, so llama.cpp auto-fits. That is correct for a model that fits\nand silently wrong for one that does not. On the 16 GB card, dense\n`Qwen3.6-27B` and `gemma-4-31B` at Q8_0 do not fit; llama.cpp placed them on CPU\nand served at 1.72 and 1.25 tok/s, in a directory asserting otherwise. The only\nrecord is one log line, `layer 0 is assigned to device CPU`.","range":{"byteOffset":{"start":19387,"end":19837},"start":{"line":396,"column":0},"end":{"line":401,"column":60}},"file":"/tmp/aimee-s1-b06-production-5ox9qqoh/work/bench/tier-a/MEASUREMENT_LOG.md","lines":"`sweep_b.sh gpu` and `sweep.sh`'s llamacpp arm write to a directory named `gpu`\nand pass no `-ngl`, so llama.cpp auto-fits. That is correct for a model that fits\nand silently wrong for one that does not. On the 16 GB card, dense\n`Qwen3.6-27B` and `gemma-4-31B` at Q8_0 do not fit; llama.cpp placed them on CPU\nand served at 1.72 and 1.25 tok/s, in a directory asserting otherwise. The only\nrecord is one log line, `layer 0 is assigned to device CPU`.","charCount":{"leading":0,"trailing":0},"language":"Markdown"}
{"text":"See the Tier-B commit for the full case. `run_b.py --max-tokens` defaulted to\n1024 while production allows `CURATOR_SYNTH_OUTBUF` (16384). With thinking left\non, models spend 400-1000 tokens reasoning before a short answer, so\n`gemma-4-12B` truncated on one topic and scored zero on it. That single row moved\nits format rate 1.0 -> 0.833 and coverage 1.0 -> 0.75, and I reported the result\nas a model finding because it fit a pattern I already believed.","range":{"byteOffset":{"start":20571,"end":21024},"start":{"line":416,"column":0},"end":{"line":421,"column":63}},"file":"/tmp/aimee-s1-b06-production-5ox9qqoh/work/bench/tier-a/MEASUREMENT_LOG.md","lines":"See the Tier-B commit for the full case. `run_b.py --max-tokens` defaulted to\n1024 while production allows `CURATOR_SYNTH_OUTBUF` (16384). With thinking left\non, models spend 400-1000 tokens reasoning before a short answer, so\n`gemma-4-12B` truncated on one topic and scored zero on it. That single row moved\nits format rate 1.0 -> 0.833 and coverage 1.0 -> 0.75, and I reported the result\nas a model finding because it fit a pattern I already believed.","charCount":{"leading":0,"trailing":0},"language":"Markdown"}
